# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_recall_integrity.py" "RECALL INTEGRITY GATE: PASS" "recall integrity (additive high-trust measurement views are correct + content-free)" "recall-integrity: additive high-trust measurement views layered on the AI-era panel WITHOUT changing any legacy metric (tests/recall_integrity.py). Issue #721's history proved the pooled MICRO-average is not reproducible (every reclone drifted the denominator 18028->18110 and even changed the evaluable set) and is dominated by one repo's giant correction commits (on the pinned 2026-07-20 panel pipeshub-ai is 61% of pairs, so micro combined 20.7% while macro is 31.1% and median 29.8%). This gate proves the LOGIC of the additive views deterministically WITHOUT git/Postgres/network on tiny synthetic inputs: (1) COMMIT-SIZE WEIGHTING gives each correction commit total weight 1 with its C(n,2) pairs sharing it, so one 20-file commit cannot outvote small commits -- proven where weighted recall is 50% while the pair-micro on the same data is 0.52%; (2) weight ACCUMULATES across commits and total_weight == #commits; (3) the UNION property holds under weighting (weighted(graph u co-change) >= max parts); (4) MECHANICAL corrections (rename/format/lint/bump/regenerate subjects) are excluded from the high-confidence 2..5-file panel while real bug/hotfix/revert subjects are kept; (5) the UNKNOWN-AWARE split partitions incident pairs into warned / at-least-unknown (a dampened extracted edge exists so the engine renders 'unknown', never a false 'clear') / clear-blind (no edge at all = the true anchor-less blind spot), with not_clear = warned + unknown; (6) MACRO/MEDIAN are the mean/median of per-repo percentages so each repo counts equally; (7) pair enumeration is deterministic (order-independent). CONTENT-FREE is structurally enforced: the gate asserts tests/recall_integrity.py opens NO repo file (no open/read_text/read_bytes), uses git --name-only (paths) + %s (commit SUBJECT only, for the boolean correction/mechanical pattern) and NEVER requests commit bodies (%b) or diffs (-p/--patch/-u). The pinned PANEL_MANIFEST (exact HEAD SHA + evaluable-incident count per repo, frozen 2026-07-20) is asserted well-formed so a later run can prove it measured the SAME corpus, not a drifted reclone. Honest boundary: these are ADDITIVE views; the legacy micro number stays the comparison anchor and no legacy metric is deleted or loosened." "recall-integrity additive views are correct and content-free: commit-size weighting (each commit total weight 1, big commits cannot dominate; weighted 50% vs pair-micro 0.52% on the same data), weight accumulation, union-under-weighting, mechanical-commit exclusion from the high-confidence 2..5-file panel, the warned/at-least-unknown/clear-blind split (not_clear = warned+unknown, never a false clear), macro/median per-repo, deterministic pair enumeration, a well-formed pinned exact-SHA manifest, and a content-free source posture (git --name-only/%s only, no open()/%b/patch)." 20
